                <pb facs="0800" n="698" xml:id="pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1153 St 2/–: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hammond</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-01T14:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 1,
                                1927—2 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 1—12:32
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>132. Department’s telegram 94, November 22, 6 p.m. The Spanish Government, acting
                    for oil monopoly, has seized without compensation Alicante installations of
                    Standard Oil subsidiary by order effective today. I have informed Spanish
                    Government that I am aware of seizure and that I am reserving all rights in the
                    premises.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hammond</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
